# The light tables and the gallery pictures live in Git LFS, and the site is deployed by GitHub Actions.
#
# The two are coupled. Pages does not resolve LFS pointers, so serving site/ straight off a branch would hand the
# page about 130 bytes of pointer text where it expects a table or a picture. .github/workflows/pages.yml checks
# out with the LFS objects pulled and uploads real files, so Pages never reads the repository itself. If the deploy
# ever moves back to a branch, these files come out of LFS in the same change.
#
# The tables are stored gzipped, which is a twelfth of their size, and unpacked by the page as they arrive.
#
# The LFS lines come last, so their -text wins over anything above them.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.wasm binary
*.gz binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
site/data/versions/*/light.json.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
site/data/gallery/**/*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
